A destroy that clears the capabilities to the pool and its objects
but not the slots its tables hold
leaves those slots in the rings of slots that survive,
and those rings then lead into memory that is the Untyped's again,
or, where a pool's own node hangs below an Untyped one of its tables holds, as the boot pool's does,
lead the destroy's last step out of RAM.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: child link to a slot that is not a live, filled one
Report: parent's ring does not reach the slot
Report: the kernel reached outside RAM

